# Companion Scan configuration (documentation only — none of these are required).
# Vite reads process.env; the Deno server reads Deno.env. Export them in your
# shell or a systemd EnvironmentFile (see docs/DEPLOY.md); .env files are NOT
# loaded automatically.

# HTTPS hostname phones use to reach this machine. Auto-detected from
# `tailscale status --json` (or a <host>.ts.net.crt in the repo root) when unset.
#TAILSCALE_HOSTNAME=your-machine.your-tailnet.ts.net
# Same value, checked second (after TAILSCALE_HOSTNAME) by both main.ts's
# resolveHostname() and vite.config.ts's — set this instead if your deploy
# tooling names the variable VITE_HOSTNAME rather than TAILSCALE_HOSTNAME.
#VITE_HOSTNAME=your-machine.your-tailnet.ts.net

# Origin prefix accepted by the Deno server's CORS check and used for share
# links. Defaults to https://$TAILSCALE_HOSTNAME, else the historical dev host.
#ALLOWED_ORIGIN_PREFIX=https://your-machine.your-tailnet.ts.net

# Deno API server port (default 8000) and the target the Vite proxy forwards
# to (default http://localhost:8000) — override both to run isolated instances.
#PORT=8000
#API_TARGET=http://localhost:8000

# Vite dev/preview server port (default 5173). Read by main.ts (share/QR links),
# vite.config.ts (server.port/preview.port), scripts/qr.mjs, scripts/house-links.mjs,
# scripts/logs-watch.mjs, and playwright.config.ts's default base URL — same
# variable, same default, everywhere. Override to run an isolated instance.
#VITE_PORT=5173

# Where the Deno server reads/writes persisted state. Defaults are relative to
# the server's cwd; override to point at a different data volume.
#SCANS_DIR=./scans
#SUMMARIES_DIR=./summaries
#SESSIONS_DIR=./scans/sessions
#WORLDS_DIR=./worlds
# projects.json path (Project metadata for the World Editor's project picker).
#PROJECTS_FILE=./projects.json
# Reference photos and other Project-scoped media (POST /projects/:id/reference-photos).
# Defaults under SCANS_DIR so a single data-volume override still catches it.
#PROJECT_MEDIA_DIR=./scans/projects

# Security: world routes (owner/editor/viewer/scanner share-link auth) allow
# anonymous access by default — set to 1 to require a valid per-world member
# token on every route that doesn't explicitly allow anonymous. Off by default
# for solo/dev use; turn on for any shared or multi-tenant deployment.
#WORLD_STRICT_AUTH=1

# A scan whose geo distance from the world's origin exceeds this radius
# (meters) is not rejected — it's placed at a fallback grid position and
# flagged geoOutlier so the viewer can call it out instead of silently
# scattering scans across a huge, wrongly-placed world.
#WORLD_SCAN_MAX_RADIUS_M=250

# Log every CORS origin check to the console (origin seen vs. ALLOWED_ORIGIN_PREFIX).
# Noisy — leave off unless debugging a rejected phone/browser origin.
#DEBUG_CORS=1

# Inference engine: ollama (default) | onnx | mock
#INFERENCE_MODE=ollama
#OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434
#OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen3-vl:4b

# Context window for the ollama call (default 8192). Left unset, ollama uses the
# model's full window — 262144 for qwen3-vl:4b — which reserves ~44 GB of KV
# cache and spills onto CPU, turning a ~20 s capture into 100+ s.
#OLLAMA_NUM_CTX=8192

# Experimental WebRTC live view. Disabled by default because the current
# device-to-editor connection is not reliable. This flag gates both the scanner
# and editor UI and makes the Deno signaling route return 404 while it is off.
#VITE_ENABLE_WEBRTC_LIVE=false

# Experimental Place Composer, which manages buildings, floors, rooms, and
# place relationships from the Spatial Editor. Disabled until that workflow is
# ready for general use.
#VITE_ENABLE_PLACE_COMPOSER=false

# /infer request cap in bytes (default 12000000)
#INFER_MAX_IMAGE_BYTES=12000000

# ONNX inference-mode model/tokenizer paths (unused in the default "ollama"
# mode). Normally set only by the Dockerfile/systemd unit alongside a mounted
# model volume — leave unset for dev.
#MODEL_DIR=./public/models/LiquidAI/LFM2.5-VL-1.6B-ONNX/onnx/
#TOKENIZER_DIR=./public/models/LiquidAI/LFM2.5-VL-1.6B-ONNX/

# Pre-built static viewer bundle main.ts falls through to in production (Docker
# / Hub install). Normally set only by the Dockerfile/systemd unit — leave
# unset for dev, where Vite serves the UI directly.
#STATIC_DIR=./dist

# Playwright: base URL for browser tests (defaults to https://$TAILSCALE_HOSTNAME:5173)
#VITE_URL=https://your-machine.your-tailnet.ts.net:5173
# Chromium binary override for hosts where `npx playwright install` is unsupported
#CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH=~/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium-1217/chrome-linux64/chrome
# Test-only Deno test gate (splat_train.test.ts) — set to 1 to run the real
# end-to-end Brush training test instead of skipping it. Not read by the
# server; irrelevant unless you're running `deno task test` with a built
# brush-cli on a GPU box.
#BRUSH_E2E=1

# ── 4D person capture ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The 4d-capture subsystem (subsystems/4d-capture/) — the ONLY config here that
# points at a machine other than this one. It needs a CUDA GPU with ~44 GiB on a
# single device; no host on the current fleet qualifies, so unset is the expected
# state today. Unset is fully supported: person-4d-reconstruct jobs complete as
# 'skipped' with a remediation hint, exactly like BRUSH_BIN and LINGBOT_MAP_*.
#FDANYONE_HOST=https://gpu-box.your-tailnet.ts.net:9040
#FDANYONE_TOKEN=
# Synthesized views per orbit layer. MUST be divisible by 4 or 6 — validated
# before the job is submitted, because a bad value fails deep inside the model.
#FDANYONE_VIEWS_PER_LAYER=6
# Timesteps sliced per second of clip. Sequence length = duration x this, and
# each timestep costs a full splat train, so this is the cost budget.
# ADOPTED, NOT MEASURED — revisit after the first real run.
#FDANYONE_TIMESTEP_FPS=5
#FDANYONE_POLL_MS=15000
#FDANYONE_MAX_WAIT_MS=2700000
# Base URL the subsystem fetches clips from. Defaults to this server's Tailscale
# name on $PORT; set it when the subsystem reaches this host by another name.
#FDANYONE_CALLBACK_BASE=https://this-box.your-tailnet.ts.net:8000

# Upload caps. INGEST_MAX_VIDEO_BYTES also bounds a person clip, which is kept
# on disk rather than discarded after keyframe extraction — see
# docs/pipelines/4d-person.md for the growth characteristic.
#INGEST_MAX_VIDEO_BYTES=1500000000
#INGEST_MAX_PHOTOS_BYTES=500000000

# LingBot-Map reconstruction worker (optional; jobs report a hint when unset)
#LINGBOT_MAP_PYTHON=~/.venvs/lingbot-map/bin/python
#LINGBOT_MAP_MODEL_PATH=~/models/lingbot-map/checkpoint.pt
# Override the worker script location main.ts spawns (default:
# scripts/lingbot_map_worker.py next to main.ts) — useful for read-only deploys.
#LINGBOT_MAP_SCRIPT=./scripts/lingbot_map_worker.py

# Bearer tokens for android-remote-control-mcp (docs/DEVICE_TESTING.md — Remote-
# controlled testing section), read from each device's Settings → Access. Every
# device runs its own server with its own token, so there is one variable per
# device — a single shared ANDROID_MCP_TOKEN cannot work across the fleet.
# Only needed when Claude Code drives on-device testing over that connector.
# Set these as persistent user/shell environment variables (not a one-off
# `export`) before launching Claude Code, so .mcp.json's ${...} placeholders
# resolve and survive session restarts — see DEVICE_TESTING.md. A
# .mcp.local.json file is gitignored but Claude Code does not automatically
# merge it with .mcp.json, so it is not a working override mechanism today.
# Never commit the real values, and never hardcode them into the tracked
# .mcp.json.
#ANDROID_MCP_TOKEN_TAB_S8_ULTRA=
#ANDROID_MCP_TOKEN_TAB_S9_ULTRA=
#ANDROID_MCP_TOKEN_BEAM_PRO_1=
#ANDROID_MCP_TOKEN_BEAM_PRO=
# Optional SenseNova-Vision worker running in WSL. Install with
# scripts/setup-sensenova-wsl.sh, then restart the Deno coordinator. Paths
# below are examples — point them at wherever setup-sensenova-wsl.sh put the
# checkout and model on your machine.
#SENSENOVA_DIR=/path/to/SenseNova-Vision
#SENSENOVA_MODEL_PATH=/path/to/models/SenseNova-Vision-7B-MoT
#SENSENOVA_BASH=C:\Windows\System32\wsl.exe

# ── Panoptic scan (optional GPU) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-keyframe panoptic segmentation: every pixel labelled, so a scan yields
# both discrete objects and room surfaces. Unset -> the job reports 'skipped'
# with a remediation, exactly like BRUSH_BIN and SPLAT_DETECT_*.
# Setup + model/licence notes: docs/pipelines/panoptic-scan.md
#PANOPTIC_PYTHON=~/.venvs/panoptic/bin/python
#PANOPTIC_DIR=~/panoptic
#PANOPTIC_MODEL=facebook/mask2former-swin-large-ade-panoptic
#PANOPTIC_MAX_FRAMES=64
